From 296f00efd15810ff126ea19bd7412caba7d90360 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your_Name <you@example.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:46:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau: clear the channel of a fence found signalled on
 enable

nouveau_fence_no_signaling() takes a fence that has already signalled off
its channel's pending list, but leaves fence->channel set. The channel
teardown clears fence->channel only for the fences still on that list, so
this one keeps pointing at the channel after it is freed. A buffer can
still hold the fence in its reservation object: when another channel then
submits work on that buffer, nouveau_fence_sync() dereferences the freed
channel. A Wayland compositor that waits on a client's buffers and keeps
compositing them after the client exits hits this as a NULL pointer
dereference in nouveau_fence_sync().

Clear fence->channel there too, as nouveau_fence_signal() does.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
index edbe9e0..cfdb946 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
@@ -487,7 +487,9 @@ static bool nouveau_fence_no_signaling(struct dma_fence *f)
 	 * just not right away.
 	 */
 	if (nouveau_fence_is_signaled(f)) {
+		/* Off the pending list, the channel teardown no longer clears it */
 		list_del(&fence->head);
+		rcu_assign_pointer(fence->channel, NULL);
 
 		dma_fence_put(&fence->base);
 		return false;
